    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Mullery O’Gara are pleased to present 49 Mountpleasant Avenue Upper to the market. A handsome red brick Victorian, bay-windowed family home extending to c. 145 sq. m. / 1560 sq. ft. Enviable location between Ranelagh and Rathmines villages. Sympathetically restored and thoughtfully enhanced by its current owners, presented in turnkey condition and seamlessly blending elegant original period features with contemporary comfort and benefits from from a sunny southerly aspect, off-street parking and an EV charger.  \r\n\r\nThe accommodation offers a superb balance of gracious reception rooms and generous double bedrooms with the renovated kitchen/dining extension forming the heart of the home. Flooded with natural light and designed to maximise the southerly aspect, glazed doors open directly onto the rear garden creating a seamless indoor-outdoor flow that is ideal for everyday family living and effortless entertaining. \r\n\r\nElegantly proportioned and briefly comprising of entrance hallway with stained glass door, ceiling cornice and stained timber floor, there is a guest w.c off the hallway. To the front is the lounge with bay window, marble mantlepiece, ceiling cornice, and stained timber floor. The living room is to the rear with marble mantlepiece, ceiling cornice, stained timber floor, bespoke alcove cabinetry and opening to the extension to the rear. \r\n\r\nStep down from the living to the open plan and spacious kitchen/dining room with exposed brick wall, exposed wooden beams and crittal style doors and window overlooking the rear garden. The kitchen itself has a wide range of shaker style units, Belfast sink, bank of larder units and island unit with additional breakfast bar seating all finished with a quartz worktop, upstand and splashback. \r\n\r\nUpstairs on the return is bedroom 1 with solid wood floors and standalone four claw bath. On the first floor are a further three bedrooms – bedroom 2 is to the rear with fitted wardrobe and shelving, cast iron mantlepiece and painted timber floor. Bedroom 3 is positioned to the front with fitted wardrobes, cast iron mantlepiece and painted timber floor. Bedroom 4 also to the front has a painted timber floor and dado rail. The newly renovated shower room completes the internal accommodation with walk in shower, w.c, whb with additional storage, tiled floor and tiled walls.  \r\n\r\nOutside to the front is a low maintenance front garden with mature hedging offering a great degree of privacy. To the rear is a wonderful south-west facing garden laid out in low maintenance paving and raised planting. There is a store off the garden and vehicular gate to Gulistan Terrace. \r\n\r\nMountpleasant Avenue Upper is positioned within minutes of Rathmines and Ranelagh villages and within walking distance of Dublin 2. The convenience cannot be overstated with an extensive range of eateries, cafes and shops on your doorstep. There is an excellent choice of both primary and secondary schools in the area including Ranelagh Multidenominational, Scoil Bhríde, Sandford Park, St. Mary’s, Alexandra College, Muckross Park and Gonzaga College to name a few. The property is beside the LUAS and numerous bus routes providing easy access to the city centre and to The Grand Canal."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Entrance Hall \r\nStained glass door and side panels, ceiling cornice, picture rail, stained timber floor and understairs storage, \r\n\r\nGuest w.c, \r\nW.c, whb, part panelled walls and tiled floor. \r\n\r\nLounge\r\nBay window, stained timber floor, black marble mantlepiece with cast iron insert and tiled hearth. Ceiling cornice and centre rose.\r\n\r\nLiving room\r\nWhite marble mantlepiece with cast iron insert, stained timber floor, ceiling cornice and centre rose. Bespoke alcove shelving and cabinets. Opening to the extension to rear. \r\n\r\nKitchen/dining\r\nTiled floor throughout. \r\nDining \r\nExposed brick wall and crittal style sliding door to rear garden. \r\nKitchen \r\nRange of shaker style units with quartz worktop, upstand and splashback. Earthenware sink, plumbed for dishwasher. Island unit with further storage and seating with quartz worktop. Velux window, pitched roof with exposed wooden beams and exposed brick wall. \r\n\r\nUpstairs\r\nReturn\r\nBedroom 1 \r\nFour claw stand-alone bath, recessed lights, access to attic, solid wood floor and hot press.\r\n\r\nFirst floor \r\nBedroom 2 (Rear)\r\nFitted wardrobes and shelving, dado rail, cast iron mantlepiece, painted timber floor and recessed lights.\r\n\r\nBedroom 3 (Front)\r\nFitted wardrobes and shelving, dado rail, cast iron mantlepiece. painted timber floor and recessed lights. \r\n\r\nBedroom 4 (Front)\r\nStained timber floor, access to attic and dado rail.\r\n\r\nShowerroom\r\nFully tiled with walk in shower featuring rainfall and telephone attachments, w.c, vanity whb with storage, vanity light, towel radiator, medicine cabinet and recessed lights. \r\n\r\nOutside\r\nRailed front garden, with paved pathway, gravel and mature hedging. Low maintenance south-west paved garden to rear. Automatic gate to Gulistan Terrace for car access. Covered side area with C.H., boiler and electric charger."
